.DS_Store

caver.jar
lib/*.jar

# Structure data and run outputs: large, and not ours to redistribute.
*.pse
*.ccp4
out_*/
output-complex*/
# examples/*/input/ is NOT ignored: the worked example's two prepared
# structures are committed (848 KB, PDB-derived) so that the first command in
# the README runs on a clean clone. Other example inputs still are.
examples/*/output/

# CAVER is GPL-3 and downloaded by the user; not ours to commit
vendor/

# Agent configuration. The skill under .claude/skills/ is a DEVELOPMENT
# practices document written for this project's own authors: it names
# internal project trees, private sibling skills and cluster operations
# that mean nothing to anyone outside the group. The public-facing half of
# it is CONTRIBUTING.md. Committing .claude/ is the normal convention for a
# team repo; this one is excluded on content, not on principle.
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# The iMARS example set is reproducible rather than bundled: its structures
# are deposited entries that `examples/iMARS/run_examples.py fetch` pulls,
# and everything else under it is computed. The two decision tables, the 19
# pair files and the script ARE committed -- the decisions, not the data.
examples/iMARS/_entries/
examples/iMARS/*/input/
examples/iMARS/*/output/
examples/iMARS/report.tsv
